<section class="standard">
  <div class="wrap standard__wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Submission received</p>
    <h1>Thank you. We have your regret.</h1>
    <p class="dek">
      It will be read, in due course, by a person who has read many such regrets and is,
      by all accounts, holding up. We&rsquo;ll be in touch only if we need to clarify a
      detail or, much more rarely, if we want to publish it.
    </p>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        In the meantime, you may wish to:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Go for a short walk.</li>
        <li>Re-read what you submitted, just the once, and then close the tab.</li>
        <li>Resist the urge to email us a follow-up explaining the bit you forgot.
          (We have all done this. None of us recommend it.)</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What happens next</h2>
      <p>
        Submissions are reviewed by the rotating editorial committee. We aim to respond
        within a fortnight, but our schedule is, on principle, also one of our regrets.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p class="hero__cta" style="margin-top: 32px;">
      <a class="btn" href="/">&larr; back to the archive</a>
      <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/contribute/">Submit another (already?)</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
